  "challenge": "ESCALATE is unnecessary because AR-004 alone makes the invoice unpayable as presented: subtotal + tax is $15,635 and the stated total is $15,525 with no line, note, additional charge, or correction explaining the $110 gap, so the correct AP disposition is REJECT and request a corrected rebill rather than ask a clerk to guess at an undeclared discount. MegaWidgets Corp is an active master vendor since 2021-11-02 with reference-exact unit prices on all three lines, but get_vendor_invoice_history returns zero prior invoices and get_prior_invoice finds no prior INV-1007, so there is no established pattern of intentional undercharges to credit. PO-001’s manager-approval path applies to otherwise-valid over-threshold bills; it does not obligate human review of an arithmetically broken one. The two IN-003 shortages (WidgetA 20 vs stock 15, WidgetB 15 vs stock 10; GadgetX ok at 3/5) further support not booking the liability until the vendor resubmits quantities and totals that can actually be fulfilled.",
  "proposed_outcome": "REJECT",
  "cites_finding_codes": ["AR-004", "IN-003", "PO-001"]
}
